{#- Share This Article: in-page share bar inside the article body. Same bare container > component
    markup as Related Articles' "Show in Page" rendering (partials/PageContent/RelatedContent.njk),
    styled by css/Article/article-share-this.css, behavior in js/Article/article-share-dock.js.
    Enhancement, no production analog.

    Two roles (proposed Sitecore model):
      - The bar (default): placed by the editor anywhere in the article body. Sticks to the top of
        the window once scrolled to.
      - The dock ({% set shareDock = true %} before the include): an empty marker built into the
        layout as the last child of the article body container. When the pinned bar reaches it,
        the bar moves into the page there and scrolls with it, until the reader scrolls back above
        the bar's original position. Takes no space itself.
    The bar and the dock must be direct children of the same container (no class needed on it):
    sticky only works inside its parent. -#}
{% if shareDock %}
<div class="share-this-article-dock"></div>
{% else %}
<div class="share-this-article">
  <div class="share-this-article__container">
    <p class="share-this-article__text"><strong>Enjoying this article?</strong> Share it &mdash;</p>
    {% include "partials/Article/ArticleShareIcons.njk" %}
  </div>
</div>
{% endif %}
